// bootstrap/aster.ast — the bootstrap compiler, stage by stage.
//
// M3d (v0.23.46-dev): the code generator. Reads one Aster source from stdin,
// writes one AArch64 ELF (ET_EXEC) to stdout, one program per run — qemu runs
// it directly. The contract is bootstrap/CODEGEN-SPEC.md; the differential
// oracle is tests/codegen-twin.c; the suite is tests/codegen-checks.sh. The
// M3c semantic pass it is built on is bootstrap/SEMANTIC-SPEC.md.
//
// Built by the host compiler, linked against nothing (M4, #216):
//   aster build-elf bootstrap/aster.ast -o aster.bin
//   aster.bin < source.ast > out.elf
// (or build-obj + link-obj as a single object — the same thing; the stage is
// self-contained, so there is no library to link.)
//
// The GENERATED regions below are owned by the bootstrap generators: the
// token kinds and the keyword chain by gen_lexer_names.py, the node kinds,
// type tags and node name tables by gen_parser_names.py. Each comes from one
// list there, shared with its C twin. Edit those, not this.
//
// Shape of the program: read_source fills srcbuf and checks the size limit;
// lex scans it into the parallel token arrays; the parser walks those tokens
// into the AST pool (two phases, so an error leaves stdout empty); the
// emitter writes the dump through outbuf. Lexer state — cursor, line, column
// — lives in globals because the scanner is one long decision chain and
// Aster has no structs to bundle it in yet. The parser's expression machine
// keeps its work stacks in fixed arrays for the same reason, and because a
// recursive-descent expression parser would spend one 8 KiB frame per
// precedence level (PARSER-SPEC.md §7).

// M4 (#216): this stage is self-contained. It used to declare four `extern fn`
// (strlen/utoa/itoa/memcmp) and take them from std.o at link time — but a
// standalone ET_EXEC cannot reference an external symbol, so the stage could
// never compile its own source: its own first extern call hit CODEGEN-SPEC §10
// C9. The routines are now written here, in the stage's own subset
// (immediately above bputraw, the emitter that consumes them), and the stage
// links against nothing at all. `strlen` was declared but never called, so it
// is gone; `reverse_digits` comes along because utoa ends by calling it.

// ---- BEGIN GENERATED: lexer names (bootstrap/gen_lexer_names.py) ----
